    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468-a5">

                <pb facs="0841" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg741"/>

                <p rendition="#center">(Copy, No. 3.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Republic, Department of War and Marine,
                        Section</hi> 1.</p>
                <p>General Abraham Plata reports to this department to-day, by telegraph, the
                    following: “In a telegram, which I received last night, the colonel of the
                    second corps of auxiliaries reports to me the following from Anganqueo: ‘Order
                    restored; tumult between operatives and American company, the result being three
                    Americans and five operatives killed. I will give you a detailed report by mail.
                    I await your orders.”</p>
                <p>“I directed said officer to remain at that point until further orders.”</p>
                <p>And I inclose it to you for your information.</p>
                <p>Liberty in the Constitution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Mexico</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1880-03-16">March 16, 1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> By order of the minister.<lb/><signed>MONTESINOS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of Foreign Affairs</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Present.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
